Hello Mesa Electrical Field Services,

Please carry out work order WO-1 on INV-3 (reseat_comms_card).

Steps, in order:
  1. Lockout and tagout the dedicated breaker supplying power to INV-3 per el=
ectrical safety procedures
  2. Verify zero energy at the inverter cabinet terminals using a calibrated =
multimeter
  3. Apply personal protective grounds on the breaker side as required by NFP=
A 70E
  4. Ensure trained personnel are standing by at the scene for emergency resp=
onse
  5. De-isolate INV-3 from the grid and lock out/tag out the AC and DC discon=
nects.
  6. Open the inverter cabinet and visually inspect the communication card fo=
r any signs of burns, loose harnesses, or corrosion.
  7. Carefully unplug the fiber and Ethernet cables from the comms card, noti=
ng their positions.
  8. Remove the communication card from its slots and reseat it firmly until =
it clicks into place.
  9. Reconnect all fiber and Ethernet cables to their original ports on the r=
eseated card.
  10. Close the cabinet, restore AC and DC power, and power-cycle INV-3.
  11. Ping the unit from SCADA to verify comms are restored and the display s=
hows live data.
  12. If the display remains dark or ping fails, re-open the cabinet and doub=
le-check all cable connections.
  13. Log the repair and update the SCADA asset status to 'online'.
  14. Remove personal protective grounds only after confirming safe conditions
  15. Re-energize the system by closing breaker 52-In supplying INV-3
  16. Restore only the communications task logs after successful verification
  17. Conduct final lockout release only after supervisory sign-off

Do not:
  - Do not attempt to power-cycle the unit before reseating the card, as this=
 may mask a loose connection.
  - Do not force the fiber cables; ensure ends are clean before reinsertion.
  - Do not ignore a persistently dark display after reseating; further hardwa=
re replacement may be needed.

